OurSync - third-party parts

OurSync contains none. It is shell script, and the Debian package it builds carries nothing but
those scripts, their templates and their documentation. Nothing is vendored, fetched at build time
or statically linked, so there is no third-party source in this repository and no third-party code
in the binary package.

What it needs at run time, and does not distribute:

  rclone              MIT      the mount, the union and the transfers. OurSync is a layer over it:
                               `rclone mount` of a union remote, `rclone copyto` for a pin, and
                               `rclone rc` to invalidate the mount's directory cache. Debian's
                               package relationship is a dependency, which is what the GNU General
                               Public License asks of a program in a separate process.
  fuse3 (fusermount3) GPL-2+   unmounting, through rclone.
  Nemo                GPL-2+   the right-click entries, which are two small .nemo_action files of
                               OurSync's own. Nemo itself is unmodified and optional.
  Google Drive                 the service the files live on. Google's API terms apply to the OAuth
                               client each user creates in their own Google Cloud project; OurSync
                               ships no client ID and asks for no credential of its own.
